        {
          "text": "Installation offers two paths: install requirements.txt followed by pip install ., or set EXLLAMA_NOCOMPILE for a JIT-mode installation. setup.py uses the presence of that environment variable—not its value—to disable precompilation. Otherwise, when Torch is already available, it gathers C/C++/CUDA sources into a CUDAExtension built through PyTorch. The README also permits running scripts directly from the checkout. It requires FlashAttention-2, reports no release builds or ROCm support, and identifies cache quantization and tensor parallelism as missing; a HIP compiler flag in setup.py does not establish working ROCm support.",
