        {
          "text": "dynamic_gen.py demonstrates queueing many prompts against a shared 32768-token cache, a batch limit of 16, and 2048-token prefill chunks. Its comment states the tradeoff: smaller chunks reduce pauses when jobs start but sacrifice prompt-ingestion throughput. async_generator.py instead wraps jobs as async iterators gathered concurrently, explicitly cancels one early-exited job, and closes the generator. banned_strings.py contrasts jobs with and without phrase suppression and displays suppressed_text separately; it also changes min_new_tokens between those conditions, so it is a feature demonstration rather than a controlled comparison.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_b26d0c0066c545de9a3937345fcc8a8b", "call_a17f1195bae7453d93d26775c14a1880", "call_dd22cd22e9fd4d388f594dc1a262ea84"]
