        {
          "text": "eval/compare_q.py separates dataset preparation from backend loading and forwarding through named function tables. Dataset and perplexity functions use disk-cache decorators; --clear_cache invalidates selected test_ppl entries. Model specifications are JSON arrays, despite the CLI help saying JSONL, and wildcard filenames can combine them. The runner emits JSON results and optionally plots perplexity against decoder bits per weight or decoder-plus-head storage. Unlike ppl.py, it does not slice the logits vocabulary before softmax. The supplied Wikitext specifications use length 2048 and stride 512, capped at 20 or 100 windows.",
