          "evidence": ["call_2daf930a08484ddd86794564f60f9d70", "call_3d36342c31f649b6bd61a360d92a9fe4", "call_618c2d9afbf840db981f5b9c4fbe8431", "call_bb74ed980c314a41ac907b2269ae4d6a"]
        },
        {
          "text": "A bounded Python check reproduced the window-target indexing. Assuming enough source tokens, 20 windows score 40,940 target occurrences but only 11,775 distinct target positions; 100 windows score 204,700 occurrences over 52,735 distinct positions. Maximum multiplicity is four. Thus the configured statistic weights overlapping predictions, including predictions with different available context, rather than scoring each corpus position once. This checks indexing only, not tokenization or perplexity values.",
