        {
          "text": "Backend adapters normalize their outputs to logits but retain different execution paths. ExLlamaV2 uses autosplit with a cache required for loading but not used by its evaluation forward. ExLlamaV3 loads for 2048-token output and forwards in flash_attn_nc mode; it can also overlay tensor files supplied alongside a model directory. llama.cpp resets state for each sequence, requests all logits with a 2048 context, and transfers scores to CUDA. Transformers loads in half precision on cuda:0 or device_map='auto' and receives the common token IDs. Sharing IDs controls one input variable but does not itself establish vocabulary compatibility across artifacts.",
