        },
        {
          "text": "eval/model_diff.py is a layerwise divergence diagnostic, not a language-quality score. It tokenizes Wikitext with model A's tokenizer, advances independent hidden states through zipped top-level module lists, and loads/unloads one module at a time to limit residency. It prints mean per-row Frobenius-relative error and maximum absolute difference divided by model B's row norm. Differences therefore accumulate through earlier modules; the script does not isolate each layer using identical incoming activations or assert that the two module lists match.",
