        {
          "text": "The science scripts probe narrower mechanisms. codebook_eval.py decodes all 65,536 16-bit states, prints RMS, plots a 256-bin histogram, and draws 20,000 transition pairs for each K=1..8 using ((state<<K)|new_bits)&0xFFFF. gumbel_eval.py compares GumbelSampler with softmax-plus-multinomial on one synthetic 128,256-logit distribution, using 250,000 samples and diagnostics every 10,000. Its 1e-5 floor clamps both empirical and reference probabilities; despite comments about ignoring small probabilities, those entries are not removed.",
